# IBrary Biology Content Pipeline

## Project Overview

This project implements a UDL-aligned biology content pipeline that extracts textbook content, aligns it with the Nigerian curriculum, and generates accessible learning modules via LLM.

## Quick Setup

```bash
make up                       # or: docker compose up -d
cp .env.example .env          # configure OPENAI_API_KEY at minimum
uv sync --extra dev --extra pipeline && uv pip install -e .  # pipeline extras carry the ML deps (torch/spaCy/etc.) only needed locally
alembic upgrade head          # create DB tables
python scripts/create_dynamodb_tables.py
make download-textbook        # download Biology2e-WEB.pdf (~380 MB)
```

## Architecture

- **Textbook**: `data/docs/extracted_source_content/biology/Biology2e-WEB.pdf` (OpenStax Biology 2e — not in git, download via `make download-textbook`)
- **Curriculum**: `data/docs/extracted_source_content/biology/biology_curriculum_structured.json` (topics 1-6 only, SSS 1)
- **UDL Rubric**: `data/docs/udlg3-graphicorganizer-digital-numbers-a11y.pdf` (CAST UDL Guidelines v3.0)
- **Storage**: PostgreSQL + pgvector for textbook chunks/embeddings; DynamoDB for published content; S3 for images

## Package Layout

All pipeline code lives under `src/ibrary/`:

| Module | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `config.py` | Central env-based configuration |
| `db.py` | SQLAlchemy engine/session |
| `models.py` | ORM models (Textbook, Chunk, Embedding, CuratedContent) |
| `curriculum/` | Curriculum validation, unit ID assignment |
| `textbook/` | PDF extraction (PyMuPDF), DB loading |
| `alignment/` | Embedding (OpenAI), pgvector similarity search |
| `curation/` | UDL content generation via RAG + OpenAI |
| `evaluation/` | UDL judge scoring |
| `serving/` | DynamoDB writer + FastAPI internal API |

Legacy extractors are in `src/sourceContentProcessor/` — do not add new code there.

## Curriculum Model

- Use `topic_number` only — never map to week numbers
- Subtopic = content item (`curriculum[N].content[M]`)
- Use `class`, `theme`, `theme_number` — no term concept
- Unit ID format: `bio_sss1_theme{T}_topic{N}_content{M}`

## Key Conventions

- **Idempotency**: all pipeline steps must be safe to re-run (upsert by ID, skip unchanged)
- **RAG flow**: always fetch full chunk content from PostgreSQL before calling LLM
- **DynamoDB**: only human-reviewed-and-approved content goes here
- **Prompt versioning**: track via file path + content hash (see `curation/prompts.py`)
- **Error handling**: retry LLM calls 3x with backoff; flag failures as `[Needs Review]`

## Running the Pipeline

```bash
python scripts/run_pipeline.py                       # default: extract, validate, align (no curation)
python scripts/run_pipeline.py --steps extract       # single step
python scripts/run_pipeline.py --full                # through publish (curation + judge + DynamoDB)
python scripts/run_pipeline.py --full --resume-from curate
python scripts/run_pipeline.py --full --skip-judge
```
